  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "**Description:**\n\nAvatar audio will sometimes bypass safety settings, playing audio even when it is turned off by that rank.\n\nTested in a public world with around 50 users at the time, making sure that the users are not manually shown. I could confirm the behavior by manually reloading a culprit avatar and the audio stopped and restarted.\n\n**Repro steps:**\n\n- Disable avatar audio for every rank except friends.\n\n- Enable avatar audio in the volume slider.\n\n- Go into a heavily populated instance (like a public world).\n\n- Make sure to not have anyone manually shown.\n\n**Expected behavior:**\n\n- Only friends will play avatar audio.\n\n**Current behavior:**\n\n- Some of the people in the instance will also play audio.\n\n**Attachments:**\n\nHere are my current safety settings and output log:\n\nhttps://pastebin.pl/view/5173d850",
